From a3a5539ec4f44c4765e250fa542a97c8c92d3183 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:59:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: P2P traffic and peers

Counts every P2P message, sent and received, by message type (the fixed
protocol list plus "other"), in bytes and in messages. The counts are
added where net.cpp already accounts bytes per message type, to the
recording thread's own counter shard: no lock is taken for them.

Connected peers are a gauge by direction, transport (TCP or P2P
WebSocket) and network, counted when a CNode is created and removed when
it is destroyed; connections established are counted by direction and
transport, and P2P WebSocket peers by compression and TLS. A node
remembers the series it was counted in, so its destruction removes
exactly that, even if metrics started in between.

Labels are bounded: no peer ids, addresses or user agents.

(cherry picked from commit c0872c638b0b60981ff818b65ae037f4133d8d3c)

